{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>ארך</b> (slow to anger): One who is long-suffering is of great understanding, and one who cannot bear his anger — his spirit is short, therefore he is called קצר רוח (short of spirit)." "<b>מרים אולת</b> (exalts folly): For one who is long-suffering humbles folly, but this one raises it when he becomes angry."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:50.369160849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}